Static Allocation:
Memory Region: Allocated in the Stack memory.
Time: Handled at compile-time before program execution.
Flexibility: Fixed size; cannot be changed during runtime.
Management: Managed automatically by the compiler.

Dynamic Allocation:
Memory Region: Allocated in the Heap memory.
Time: Handled at runtime while the program executes.
Flexibility: Dynamic size; can grow or shrink as needed using new and delete.
Management: Managed manually by the programmer.
